module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.CrystalDeRhamComplex

/-!
# A truncation map becomes a quasi-isomorphism after `Ru_{X/S, *}`

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` of [Stacks, Tag 07MF].  The leading
assertion of [Stacks, Tag 07LM] says that the truncation map

`(F → F ⊗_{𝒪_{X/S}} Ω¹_{X/S} → F ⊗_{𝒪_{X/S}} Ω²_{X/S} → ⋯) ⟶ F[0]`

becomes a quasi-isomorphism after `Ru_{X/S, *}`, and the source derives it from the sharper
vanishing clause of the same tag: `Ru_{X/S, *}(F ⊗ Ω^i_{X/S}) = 0` for `i > 0`.  That derivation
uses nothing about the de Rham complex beyond three facts — that the complex is an `ℕ`-indexed
complex of abelian presheaves on `Cris(X/S)`, that the truncation map to the degree-zero term is
an isomorphism in degree zero, and that `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills the sheaves generated by the terms in
positive degrees.  **This file isolates the argument at exactly that generality.**

So the data here are an `ℕ`-indexed cochain complex `K` of abelian presheaves on `Cris(X/S)`, an
abelian presheaf `L`, and a map of complexes `τ : K ⟶ L[0]` with `τ⁰` an isomorphism; the
conclusion is that `τ`, read on abelian sheaves and in `D⁺(Ab(X_Zar))`, becomes an isomorphism
after `Ru_{X/S, *}` as soon as `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills the sheaf generated by `K^i` for every
`i > 0`.  Specialised to the de Rham complex of `𝒪_{X/S}` this is
`...SmallSite.isIso_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_map_crysDeRhamTruncation` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/CrystalDeRhamComplex.lean`, which is where the
discussion of what [Stacks, Tag 07LM] does and does not owe belongs.

## The argument

Termwise sheafification at the coefficient universe `u + 1`, followed by extension of the
`ℕ`-indexing to `ℤ` by zero, is the additive functor `crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor`; it carries
`K`, `L[0]` and `τ` to `abelianSheafComplex`, `abelianSingleComplex` and `abelianSheafTruncation`,
and nothing of the mathematics happens in it.  The resulting map sits in the degreewise split
short exact sequence

`0 ⟶ σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K ⟶ K⁰[0] ⟶ 0`

(`abelianShortComplex`, split by `abelianSplitting` — in degree zero the first term vanishes and
the second map is `τ⁰`, in a degree `≥ 1` the first map is an identity and the last term
vanishes, and in a negative degree everything vanishes), hence in a distinguished triangle of
`K⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))` by [Stacks, Tag 0118] (`abelianTrianglePlus_distinguished`), which
`DerivedCategory.Plus.Qh` and the exact functor `Ru_{X/S, *}` carry to a distinguished triangle of
`D⁺(Ab(X_Zar))`.  Its first vertex is `Ru_{X/S, *}(σ^{≥1}K)`, which vanishes by Leray's acyclicity
lemma [Stacks, Tag 015E] — `isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_obj_of_termwise` — the terms
of `σ^{≥1}K` being the sheaves generated by the `K^i` with `i > 0` together with zeroes.  A
distinguished triangle whose first vertex is zero has an invertible second map.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.abelianSheafComplex`,
  `...SmallSite.abelianSingleComplex` and `...SmallSite.abelianSheafTruncation` — the complex `K`,
  the complex `L[0]` and the map `τ`, read as bounded below complexes of abelian sheaves on
  `Cris(X/S)` and a map between them.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.abelianSheafTruncGE` — the brutal truncation
  `σ^{≥1}` of `abelianSheafComplex`, the third vertex of the triangle of `τ`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.abelianShortComplex` and
  `...SmallSite.abelianTrianglePlus` — the short exact sequence `0 ⟶ σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K ⟶ K⁰[0] ⟶ 0` of
  the truncation map, and the triangle of `K⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))` it generates.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.abelianPlusComplex`,
  `...SmallSite.abelianSinglePlusComplex`, `...SmallSite.abelianPlusTruncGE`,
  `...SmallSite.abelianPlusTruncation` and `...SmallSite.abelianPlusIota` — the same four objects
  and two maps read in `C⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))`.

## Main results

* `...SmallSite.isIso_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_map_abelianPlusTruncation` — **the source's
  derivation of the leading assertion of [Stacks, Tag 07LM], with the particular complex replaced
  by a parameter**: if `τ⁰` is an isomorphism and `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills the sheaf generated by `K^i`
  for every `i > 0`, then `τ` becomes an isomorphism of `D⁺(Ab(X_Zar))` after `Ru_{X/S, *}`.
* `...SmallSite.abelianSplitting` and `...SmallSite.abelianTrianglePlus_distinguished` — the short
  exact sequence of the truncation map is degreewise split, and its triangle is distinguished.
* `...SmallSite.isIso_abelianSheafTruncation_f_zero` — the degree-zero isomorphism survives
  sheafification and the change of indexing.
* `...SmallSite.isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImage_abelianSheafTruncGE_X` — under the vanishing
  hypothesis, `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills every term of `σ^{≥1}K`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07LM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0118](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0118)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 015E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/015E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry
open Opposite

universe w w' u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})
  (K : CochainComplex ((CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u}) ℕ)
  (L : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u})
  (τ : K ⟶ (CochainComplex.single₀ ((CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u})).obj L)

namespace SmallSite

section Truncation

attribute [local instance 2000] HomotopyCategory.Plus.instHasPointwiseRightDerivedFunctorQuasiIso

variable [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]
  [HasDerivedCategory.{w'} (Sheaf (opensTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]

open Pretriangulated

/-- **The complex `K` as a bounded below complex of abelian sheaves**, the image of `K` under
`crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor`: sheafify termwise at the coefficient universe `u + 1` and extend
the `ℕ`-indexing to `ℤ` by zero. -/
def abelianSheafComplex :
    CochainComplex (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) ℤ :=
  (crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor S).obj K

/-- **`L` placed in degree zero**, as a bounded below complex of abelian sheaves: the target of
the truncation map. -/
def abelianSingleComplex :
    CochainComplex (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) ℤ :=
  (crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor S).obj
    ((CochainComplex.single₀ ((CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u})).obj L)

/-- **The truncation map `τ : K ⟶ L[0]`, on abelian sheaves**: the image of `τ` under
`crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor`.  It is the same map; only the category it is read in has
changed. -/
def abelianSheafTruncation : abelianSheafComplex S K ⟶ abelianSingleComplex S L :=
  (crysDeRhamSheafComplexFunctor S).map τ

/-- The complex `abelianSheafComplex S K` is strictly concentrated in degrees `≥ 0`: its terms in
negative degrees are zero. -/
instance abelianSheafComplex_isStrictlyGE : (abelianSheafComplex S K).IsStrictlyGE 0 :=
  inferInstanceAs (CochainComplex.IsStrictlyGE
    ((((crysAbelianSheafification S).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj K).extend
      ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat) 0)

/-- The complex `abelianSingleComplex S L` is strictly concentrated in degrees `≥ 0`: its terms in
negative degrees are zero. -/
instance abelianSingleComplex_isStrictlyGE : (abelianSingleComplex S L).IsStrictlyGE 0 :=
  inferInstanceAs (CochainComplex.IsStrictlyGE
    ((((crysAbelianSheafification S).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj
      ((CochainComplex.single₀ ((CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u})).obj L)).extend
      ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat) 0)

/-- In degree `i ≥ 0` the complex of abelian sheaves has the sheaf generated by `K^i` as its
term. -/
def abelianSheafComplexXIso (i : ℕ) :
    (abelianSheafComplex S K).X (i : ℤ) ≅ (crysAbelianSheafification S).obj (K.X i) :=
  HomologicalComplex.extendXIso _ ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (i := i) (by simp)

omit [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]
  [HasDerivedCategory.{w'} (Sheaf (opensTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})] in
/-- Outside degree zero the complex `L[0]` of abelian sheaves vanishes. -/
theorem isZero_abelianSingleComplex_X (n : ℤ) (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    IsZero ((abelianSingleComplex S L).X n) := by
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hn with h | h
  · exact HomologicalComplex.isZero_extend_X _ ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat n
      (fun i hi => by simp only [ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat_f] at hi; omega)
  · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le h.le
    refine IsZero.of_iso ?_
      (HomologicalComplex.extendXIso _ ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (i := k) (by simp))
    exact Functor.map_isZero (crysAbelianSheafification S)
      (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X (ComplexShape.up ℕ) 0 _ k (by omega))

omit [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]
  [HasDerivedCategory.{w'} (Sheaf (opensTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})] in
/-- In degree zero the truncation map of abelian sheaves is an isomorphism, as soon as `τ⁰` is:
sheafification and the change of indexing preserve the identification. -/
theorem isIso_abelianSheafTruncation_f_zero (hτ : IsIso (τ.f 0)) :
    IsIso ((abelianSheafTruncation S K L τ).f 0) := by
  have h : IsIso (τ.f 0) := hτ
  rw [show (abelianSheafTruncation S K L τ).f 0 = _ from
    HomologicalComplex.extendMap_f
      (((crysAbelianSheafification S).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).map τ)
      ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (i := 0) (by simp),
    Functor.mapHomologicalComplex_map_f]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' (Iso.isIso_hom _)
    (IsIso.comp_isIso' (Functor.map_isIso _ _) (Iso.isIso_inv _))

/-- **The brutal truncation `σ^{≥1}` of the complex of abelian sheaves**: the complex
`K¹ → K² → ⋯` of generated sheaves, placed in degrees `≥ 1`.  It is the third vertex of the
triangle of the truncation map, and the vanishing hypothesis of the leading assertion is exactly
the statement that `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills each of its terms. -/
def abelianSheafTruncGE :
    CochainComplex (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) ℤ :=
  (abelianSheafComplex S K).stupidTrunc (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1)

/-- The truncation `abelianSheafTruncGE S K` is strictly concentrated in degrees `≥ 1`: its terms
in degrees `≤ 0` are zero. -/
instance abelianSheafTruncGE_isStrictlyGE : (abelianSheafTruncGE S K).IsStrictlyGE 1 :=
  inferInstanceAs (((abelianSheafComplex S K).stupidTrunc
    (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1)).IsStrictlySupported (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1))

/-- **The short complex `0 ⟶ σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K ⟶ K⁰[0] ⟶ 0`** of abelian sheaves, whose second map is
the truncation map.  It is degreewise split as soon as `τ⁰` is an isomorphism,
`abelianSplitting`. -/
def abelianShortComplex :
    ShortComplex (CochainComplex (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) ℤ) :=
  ShortComplex.mk
    (HomologicalComplex.ιStupidTrunc (abelianSheafComplex S K)
      (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1))
    (abelianSheafTruncation S K L τ) (by
      refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n => ?_
      rw [HomologicalComplex.comp_f, HomologicalComplex.zero_f]
      by_cases hn : n = 0
      · subst hn
        exact (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE (abelianSheafTruncGE S K) 1 0
          (by omega)).eq_of_src _ _
      · exact (isZero_abelianSingleComplex_X S L n hn).eq_of_tgt _ _)

/-- **The short complex of the truncation map is degreewise split.**  In degree zero its first
term vanishes and its second map is `τ⁰`, which is assumed invertible; in a degree `≥ 1` its
first map is an identity and its last term vanishes; in a negative degree everything vanishes. -/
noncomputable def abelianSplitting (hτ : IsIso (τ.f 0)) (n : ℤ) :
    ((abelianShortComplex S K L τ).map
      (HomologicalComplex.eval _ _ n)).Splitting := by
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn
    exact ShortComplex.Splitting.ofIsZeroOfIsIso _
      (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE (abelianSheafTruncGE S K) 1 0 (by omega))
      (isIso_abelianSheafTruncation_f_zero S K L τ hτ)
  · refine ShortComplex.Splitting.ofIsIsoOfIsZero _ ?_
      (isZero_abelianSingleComplex_X S L n hn)
    by_cases hn1 : (1 : ℤ) ≤ n
    · exact HomologicalComplex.isIso_ιStupidTrunc_f _ _ (i := (n - 1).toNat)
        (by change (1 : ℤ) + ((n - 1).toNat : ℤ) = n; omega)
    · exact IsZero.isIso
        (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE (abelianSheafTruncGE S K) 1 n (by omega))
        (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE (abelianSheafComplex S K) 0 n (by omega)) _

/-! #### The distinguished triangle of the truncation map -/

/-- `σ^{≥1}K`, read as a bounded below complex of abelian sheaves. -/
def abelianPlusTruncGE :
    CochainComplex.Plus (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  ⟨abelianSheafTruncGE S K, ⟨1, inferInstance⟩⟩

/-- `K`, read as a bounded below complex of abelian sheaves. -/
def abelianPlusComplex :
    CochainComplex.Plus (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  ⟨abelianSheafComplex S K, ⟨0, inferInstance⟩⟩

/-- `L[0]`, read as a bounded below complex of abelian sheaves. -/
def abelianSinglePlusComplex :
    CochainComplex.Plus (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  ⟨abelianSingleComplex S L, ⟨0, inferInstance⟩⟩

/-- **The truncation map `τ : K ⟶ L[0]`, in `C⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))`.** -/
def abelianPlusTruncation : abelianPlusComplex S K ⟶ abelianSinglePlusComplex S L :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (abelianSheafTruncation S K L τ)

/-- The inclusion `σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K`, in `C⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))`. -/
def abelianPlusIota : abelianPlusTruncGE S K ⟶ abelianPlusComplex S K :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (HomologicalComplex.ιStupidTrunc (abelianSheafComplex S K)
    (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1))

/-- **The triangle `σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K ⟶ K⁰[0] ⟶ (σ^{≥1}K)⟦1⟧` of `K⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))`** attached to the
degreewise split short exact sequence `abelianShortComplex`.  Its second map is the truncation
map; its first vertex is the brutal truncation whose terms the vanishing hypothesis kills. -/
noncomputable def abelianTrianglePlus (hτ : IsIso (τ.f 0)) :
    Triangle (HomotopyCategory.Plus (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})) :=
  Triangle.mk
    ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).map (abelianPlusIota S K))
    ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).map (abelianPlusTruncation S K L τ))
    (ObjectProperty.homMk
      ((CochainComplex.trianglehOfDegreewiseSplit (abelianShortComplex S K L τ)
          (abelianSplitting S K L τ hτ)).mor₃ ≫
        ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).commShiftIso (1 : ℤ)).inv.app
          ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).obj (abelianPlusTruncGE S K))))

omit [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]
  [HasDerivedCategory.{w'} (Sheaf (opensTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})] in
/-- **The triangle of the truncation map is distinguished in `K⁺`.**  It is distinguished in
`K(Ab(Cris(X/S)))` by [Stacks, Tag 0118] — a degreewise split short exact sequence of complexes
gives a distinguished triangle of the homotopy category — and the inclusion `K⁺ ⥤ K` is fully
faithful and triangulated. -/
theorem abelianTrianglePlus_distinguished (hτ : IsIso (τ.f 0)) :
    abelianTrianglePlus S K L τ hτ ∈
      distTriang (HomotopyCategory.Plus (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})) := by
  rw [← Functor.map_distinguished_iff (HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _)]
  refine isomorphic_distinguished _
    (CochainComplex.trianglehOfDegreewiseSplit_distinguished (abelianShortComplex S K L τ)
      (abelianSplitting S K L τ hτ)) _
    (Triangle.isoMk _ _ (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_ ?_)
  · exact (Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
  · exact (Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
  · have h : (CategoryTheory.shiftFunctor
        (HomotopyCategory (Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)) (1 : ℤ)).map
          (Iso.refl ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).mapTriangle.obj
            (abelianTrianglePlus S K L τ hτ)).obj₁).hom = 𝟙 _ := by simp
    have h₂ : ((CochainComplex.trianglehOfDegreewiseSplit (abelianShortComplex S K L τ)
          (abelianSplitting S K L τ hτ)).mor₃ ≫
        ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).commShiftIso (1 : ℤ)).inv.app
          ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).obj (abelianPlusTruncGE S K))) ≫
        ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).commShiftIso (1 : ℤ)).hom.app
          ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).obj (abelianPlusTruncGE S K)) =
        (CochainComplex.trianglehOfDegreewiseSplit (abelianShortComplex S K L τ)
          (abelianSplitting S K L τ hτ)).mor₃ :=
      (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
        ((congrArg (fun g => (CochainComplex.trianglehOfDegreewiseSplit
            (abelianShortComplex S K L τ) (abelianSplitting S K L τ hτ)).mor₃ ≫ g)
          (Iso.inv_hom_id_app ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).commShiftIso (1 : ℤ))
            ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).obj
              (abelianPlusTruncGE S K)))).trans (Category.comp_id _))
    exact (congrArg (fun g => ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.ι _).mapTriangle.obj
        (abelianTrianglePlus S K L τ hτ)).mor₃ ≫ g) h).trans
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (h₂.trans (Category.id_comp _).symm))

/-! #### `Ru_{X/S, *}` is an exact functor of triangulated categories -/

attribute [local instance] crysCommShiftDerivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor
  crysIsTriangulatedDerivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor crysAdditiveDerivedZariskiDirectImage

/-! #### The leading assertion -/

/-- Under the vanishing hypothesis, `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills every term of `σ^{≥1}K`: in a degree
`≥ 1` the term is the sheaf generated by `K^i` with `i > 0`, which the hypothesis kills, and in
every other degree it is zero. -/
theorem isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImage_abelianSheafTruncGE_X
    (hV : ∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i → IsZero ((derivedZariskiDirectImage S).obj
      ((crysAbelianSheafification S).obj (K.X i))))
    (n : ℤ) :
    IsZero ((derivedZariskiDirectImage S).obj ((abelianSheafTruncGE S K).X n)) := by
  by_cases hn : (1 : ℤ) ≤ n
  · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k : ℕ, n = (k : ℤ) := ⟨n.toNat, by omega⟩
    refine IsZero.of_iso (hV k (by omega)) ((derivedZariskiDirectImage S).mapIso ?_)
    exact HomologicalComplex.stupidTruncXIso (abelianSheafComplex S K)
        (ComplexShape.embeddingUpIntGE 1) (i := k - 1)
        (by change (1 : ℤ) + ((k - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (k : ℤ); omega) ≪≫
      abelianSheafComplexXIso S K k
  · exact Functor.map_isZero _ (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE
      (abelianSheafTruncGE S K) 1 n (by omega))

/-- **The leading assertion of [Stacks, Tag 07LM], with the particular complex replaced by a
parameter.**  Let `K` be an `ℕ`-indexed cochain complex of abelian presheaves on `Cris(X/S)`, `L`
an abelian presheaf, and `τ : K ⟶ L[0]` a map of complexes whose degree-zero component is an
isomorphism.  If `Ru_{X/S, *}` kills the sheaf generated by `K^i` for every `i > 0`, then `τ`,
read on abelian sheaves and in `D⁺(Ab(X_Zar))`, becomes an isomorphism after `Ru_{X/S, *}` — that
is, it becomes a quasi-isomorphism.

The proof is the one the source gives.  The truncation map sits in the degreewise split short
exact sequence `0 ⟶ σ^{≥1}K ⟶ K ⟶ K⁰[0] ⟶ 0` (`abelianShortComplex`, `abelianSplitting`), hence
in a distinguished triangle of `K⁺(Ab(Cris(X/S)))` by [Stacks, Tag 0118]
(`abelianTrianglePlus_distinguished`), which `Qh` and the exact functor `Ru_{X/S, *}` carry to a
distinguished triangle of `D⁺(Ab(X_Zar))`.  Its first vertex is `Ru_{X/S, *}(σ^{≥1}K)`, which
vanishes: the terms of `σ^{≥1}K` are the sheaves generated by the `K^i` with `i > 0`, the
hypothesis `hV` kills each of them, and Leray's acyclicity lemma [Stacks, Tag 015E],
`isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_obj_of_termwise`, carries that to the complex.  A
distinguished triangle whose first vertex is zero has an invertible second map,
`Triangle.isZero₁_iff_isIso₂`.

Specialised to the de Rham complex of `𝒪_{X/S}` and its truncation map this is
`...SmallSite.isIso_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_map_crysDeRhamTruncation`, where the
standing of the two hypotheses in [Stacks, Tag 07LM] is discussed.  No tag attribute is placed
here: this is the source's *derivation*, read at a generality the tag does not state. -/
theorem isIso_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_map_abelianPlusTruncation
    (hτ : IsIso (τ.f 0))
    (hV : ∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i → IsZero ((derivedZariskiDirectImage S).obj
      ((crysAbelianSheafification S).obj (K.X i)))) :
    IsIso ((derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor S).map
      (DerivedCategory.Plus.Qh.map
        ((HomotopyCategory.Plus.quotient _).map (abelianPlusTruncation S K L τ)))) := by
  have hT := (derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor S).map_distinguished _
    (DerivedCategory.Plus.Qh.map_distinguished _
      (abelianTrianglePlus_distinguished S K L τ hτ))
  refine (Triangle.isZero₁_iff_isIso₂ _ hT).1 ?_
  exact isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImageFunctor_obj_of_termwise S (abelianPlusTruncGE S K)
    (isZero_derivedZariskiDirectImage_abelianSheafTruncGE_X S K hV)

end Truncation

end SmallSite

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

end

